137	<h2>Not yet read</h2>
138	<p>One item. The page holds only what you have not read. At 16:17 UTC on 6 November, you marked the page read up to change 35, so changes 34 and 35 left, and the new item is numbered 36.</p>
139	<p>Change 36 is not a new rule, and the rule&rsquo;s meaning did not change. The bullet on deleting branches now says that it holds in a session in a cloud container, and it points to the <code>cloud-container</code> skill for the reason. The item shows the text on <code>main</code> now, against the text before the first of its two commits, with the old words struck through and the new words underlined.</p>
